This directory only. The rest of this repository is AGPL-3.0, and `LICENSE` at
the root is the licence that governs it.

The exception is deliberate and it is what makes the iPhone app possible. Listen
for iPhone is closed source and lives in its own repository; it compiles these
files directly, so they cannot be AGPL without taking the phone app with them.
Keeping the shared half permissive is also the honest arrangement for anybody
else: this is the folder contract, the sealing and the sync protocol, and those
are more useful to the world unencumbered than they are as leverage.
